      "created_at": "2025-08-11T13:42:15Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-08-11T13:42:15Z",
      "body": "It might be nice to at least have the option to hide applications from the applications section if the user doesn\u2019t have access to them, because in most cases an application is just a link, and currently a user without permissions to create/edit applications can still see all applications created in the system, as well as the link leading to them. This is regardless of whether they are placed on boards the user has access to, or on boards they do not have access to.\n\nAlternatively, it would be great to have an access control setting for the applications section itself, so that users without a specific group membership cannot see them.\n\nOn the boards themselves, if the user has access to the board, the application could either not be hidden at all, or its icon could be replaced with a generic lock icon, making it non-clickable and hiding its name as well.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/homarr-labs/homarr/issues/comments/3174906691/reactions",
