      "created_at": "2025-09-05T21:16:11Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-09-05T21:16:11Z",
      "body": "It would be a fantastic feature to be able to completely hide apps based on user roles or groups, just as Dashy does.\n\nThis would make Homarr perfect for multi-user environments. Currently, all users can see all available apps. Ideally, a user should only see the apps they have permission to access.\n\nThis could be implemented using parameters similar to Dashy's:\n\nhideForKeycloakUsers:\nThe item is visible to all Keycloak users, except for those in the specified groups or roles.\nRef: [Dashy Docs - hideForKeycloakUsers](https://dashy.to/docs/configuring/#sectiondisplaydatahideforkeycloakusers-sectiondisplaydatashowforkeycloakusers-itemdisplaydatahideforkeycloakusers-and-itemdisplaydatashowforkeycloakusers)\n\nshowForKeycloakUsers:\nThe item is hidden from all Keycloak users, and only shown to those in the specified groups or roles.\nRef: [Dashy Docs - showForKeycloakUsers](https://dashy.to/docs/configuring/#sectiondisplaydatahideforkeycloakusers-sectiondisplaydatashowforkeycloakusers-itemdisplaydatahideforkeycloakusers-and-itemdisplaydatashowforkeycloakusers)\n\nThis granular level of control would be a game-changer!",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
